// jni-flow.bridge.jsonl -- the JniFlow boundary, joined by hand.
//
// The presence of this file makes the regression runner discover a second case,
// `Jni:JniFlow+bridge`, which indexes the same two artifacts with `--no-jni-bridge` and this
// model, then makes exactly the claims `jni-flow.json` makes. It is a direct A/B against the
// built-in pass: if the declarative construct is as expressive as the pass for this boundary,
// both cases pass identically.
//
// `--no-jni-bridge` is not optional. A user bridge over a pair the built-in pass also links
// double-bridges it -- two sites, duplicated flows -- so the case would pass for the wrong
// reason.
//
// Both natives are STATIC, so the JNI implementation takes `JNIEnv *` at index 0 and the
// declaring `jclass` at index 1; declared parameter k lands at 2 + k. The Java side is a DEX,
// which numbers parameters by *register* slot -- for a static method the first declared
// parameter is slot 0, and neither of these methods has a wide (long/double) parameter, so the
// slots and the declaration order coincide here. Write these against the artifact you are
// actually indexing: the same class imported as a `.jar` would number them differently the
// moment a `long` appeared.
//
// The globals pseudo-parameter is mapped unconditionally and is not written here. It is what
// makes this case work at all: the taint enters `nativeStash`, is held in the native global
// `g_slot`, and leaves through a *different* function, `nativeFetch`. Nothing in the Java half
// connects the two.

// nativeStash(String data) -> void. `data` is Java slot 0, native index 2.
{"find":"methods","in":{"languages":["dex","apk"]},"where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","qualified-id":"LJniFlow;->nativeStash(Ljava/lang/String;)V"}],"model":{"bridge":{"to":{"in":{"language":"pcode"},"where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","name":"Java_JniFlow_nativeStash"}]},"arguments":[{"from":"Argument(0)","to":"Argument(2)"}]}}}

// nativeFetch() -> String. No declared parameters; only the return crosses.
{"find":"methods","in":{"languages":["dex","apk"]},"where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","qualified-id":"LJniFlow;->nativeFetch()Ljava/lang/String;"}],"model":{"bridge":{"to":{"in":{"language":"pcode"},"where":[{"constraint":"signature_match","name":"Java_JniFlow_nativeFetch"}]},"arguments":[{"from":"Return","to":"Return"}]}}}
